---
/**
 * ProtonGradientBattery — a side-view cross-section of the inner mitochondrial membrane that
 * teaches ONE idea: electron flow and ATP synthesis are SEPARATE machines, coupled only by the
 * proton gradient. The respiratory chain (Complexes I→III→IV) is a pump that charges a battery;
 * ATP synthase is a motor that spends it. They never touch — the only wire between them is H+.
 *
 * Send an electron pair and watch it run down the chain (and down the redox ladder drawn beneath
 * the membrane, with rungs placed at their true E°′ so the big drops at I, III and IV are visible),
 * the pumps lift H+ into the intermembrane space, the gradient meter fill, and — once the gradient
 * is above threshold — the F1 rotor turn 120° per ATP. Flip the uncoupler and the wire is cut:
 * electrons keep flowing, O2 is still consumed, but the protons leak straight back as HEAT.
 * Inhibitors stop electron flow at one complex and show the crossover pattern on the carriers.
 *
 * Teaching-grade stoichiometry (standard textbook accounting, matching the lesson prose):
 *   H+ pumped per electron pair — Complex I = 4, Complex II = 0, Complex III = 4, Complex IV = 2.
 *   So NADH banks 10 H+ and FADH2 banks 6 H+. One pair reduces ½ O2 to H2O.
 *   ATP synthase ~4 H+/ATP (including ADP/Pi import) → ~2.5 ATP/NADH, ~1.5 ATP/FADH2.
 *   The synthase only turns while the gradient is above a threshold (it needs enough driving force
 *   to make ATP), so the first pair charges the battery and later pairs cash it in; the running
 *   average converges on 2.5 or 1.5.
 * Deterministic model; the run animation uses requestAnimationFrame and is skipped entirely under
 * prefers-reduced-motion. Self-contained vanilla-TS Astro island, no imports, no props. Original.
 */
---

<figure class="pgb card" data-pgbattery>
  <figcaption class="pgb-head">The proton gradient is a battery — charge it, spend it, or short it out<span class="pgb-chip">⚙ original · interactive</span></figcaption>

  <p class="pgb-howto">Press <strong>Send one electron pair</strong> and follow it: down the chain, down the redox ladder, H⁺ pumped up, then ATP synthase spending the gradient. Then try an inhibitor or the uncoupler.</p>

  <svg
    class="pgb-svg"
    viewBox="0 0 540 508"
    role="img"
    aria-label="Side-view cross-section of the inner mitochondrial membrane: Complexes I to IV pump protons from the matrix into the intermembrane space, ATP synthase lets them flow back to make ATP. Below, a redox ladder places each electron carrier at its reduction potential."
    data-stage
  ></svg>

  <ul class="pgb-legend" aria-hidden="true">
    <li><i class="pgb-dot pgb-dot-e"></i>electron pair</li>
    <li><i class="pgb-dot pgb-dot-h"></i>H⁺</li>
    <li><i class="pgb-dot pgb-dot-red"></i>carrier reduced (holding e⁻)</li>
    <li><i class="pgb-dot pgb-dot-ox"></i>carrier oxidized</li>
  </ul>

  <div class="pgb-meter">
    <div class="pgb-meter-top"><span>Proton gradient — the battery's charge</span><strong data-pmf-num>0 H⁺</strong></div>
    <div class="pgb-bar"><div class="pgb-bar-fill" data-bar></div><div class="pgb-bar-thresh" data-thresh></div></div>
    <div class="pgb-meter-note">The tick marks the threshold: ATP synthase turns only while the gradient is charged above it.</div>
  </div>

  <div class="pgb-readouts">
    <div class="pgb-ro"><span class="pgb-ro-name">ATP made</span><span class="pgb-ro-v pgb-pos" data-atp>0</span></div>
    <div class="pgb-ro"><span class="pgb-ro-name">O₂ consumed</span><span class="pgb-ro-v" data-o2>0</span></div>
    <div class="pgb-ro"><span class="pgb-ro-name">Heat (H⁺ leaked)</span><span class="pgb-ro-v pgb-neg" data-heat>0</span></div>
    <div class="pgb-ro"><span class="pgb-ro-name">Per pair, at 4 H⁺/ATP</span><span class="pgb-ro-v" data-yield>—</span></div>
  </div>

  <div class="pgb-controls">
    <div class="pgb-group">
      <span class="pgb-g-label">Electron entry point</span>
      <div class="pgb-seg" role="group" aria-label="Electron entry point">
        <button type="button" data-entry="NADH" aria-pressed="true">NADH (Complex I)</button>
        <button type="button" data-entry="FADH2" aria-pressed="false">FADH₂ (Complex II)</button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="pgb-group">
      <span class="pgb-g-label">Inhibitor</span>
      <div class="pgb-seg" role="group" aria-label="Respiratory chain inhibitor">
        <button type="button" data-inhib="none" aria-pressed="true">None</button>
        <button type="button" data-inhib="I" aria-pressed="false">Rotenone (I)</button>
        <button type="button" data-inhib="III" aria-pressed="false">Antimycin A (III)</button>
        <button type="button" data-inhib="IV" aria-pressed="false">Cyanide (IV)</button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="pgb-group">
      <span class="pgb-g-label">Coupling</span>
      <div class="pgb-seg" role="group" aria-label="Uncoupler">
        <button type="button" data-uncouple aria-pressed="false">DNP / proton leak: OFF</button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="pgb-actions">
      <button type="button" class="pgb-run" data-run>Send one electron pair ▸</button>
      <button type="button" class="pgb-reset" data-reset>Reset</button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="pgb-log" data-log aria-live="polite"></p>
  <p class="pgb-takeaway" data-takeaway role="status"></p>

  <p class="pgb-foot">Here is the whole chapter in one sentence: the respiratory chain and ATP synthase are <em>two different machines that never touch</em>. The chain is a pump that charges a battery (the H⁺ gradient); ATP synthase is a motor that spends it. Cut the wire between them — add an uncoupler like 2,4-dinitrophenol — and electrons still flow, O₂ is still burned, but the protons leak back as heat and almost no ATP gets made. That is exactly how brown fat keeps a newborn warm and why a fever spikes your metabolic rate. It is also why DNP, sold as a 1930s diet pill, melted fat by literally turning the battery into a space heater — and killed people by cooking them from the inside. Same physics, two destinies, decided entirely by whether the protons go through the motor.</p>
</figure>

<script>
  const ACCENT = '#0e7c86', NAVY = '#232d4b', ORANGE = '#e57200', GOLD = '#D4A843', GOLD_INK = '#7f6315';
  const INK = '#4b4b55', MUTED = '#6b6b6b', RED = '#c0392b', SLATE = '#8a93ad', FAINT = '#c9cedb';
  const SVGNS = 'http://www.w3.org/2000/svg';
  // SVG text scale: the 540-wide scene shrinks to ~60% on a phone, so enlarge its text there
  let FS = 1;
  function el(name: string, attrs: Record<string, string | number>, text?: string): SVGElement {
    const e = document.createElementNS(SVGNS, name);
    for (const k in attrs) e.setAttribute(k, String(attrs[k]));
    if (text !== undefined) e.textContent = text;
    return e;
  }

  type Entry = 'NADH' | 'FADH2';
  type Inhib = 'none' | 'I' | 'III' | 'IV';
  type Cx = 'I' | 'II' | 'III' | 'IV';

  // --- model constants -------------------------------------------------------------------
  const H_PER_ATP = 4;     // ~4 H+ per ATP including ADP/Pi transport
  const THRESH = 12;       // synthase turns only while the gradient holds more than this
  const MAX_H = 30;        // meter ceiling (max possible charge is THRESH + 3 + 10 = 25)
  const PUMP: Record<Cx, number> = { I: 4, II: 0, III: 4, IV: 2 };

  // --- scene geometry (viewBox 540 × 508) ---------------------------------------------------
  const W = 540;
  const IMS_BOT = 96, MEM_TOP = 96, MEM_BOT = 184, MAT_BOT = 300;
  const CXX: Record<Cx, number> = { I: 60, II: 145, III: 230, IV: 315 };
  const CW = 64, C_TOP = 88, C_BOT = 192;
  const E_Y = 170;                               // electron track inside the complexes
  const Q_POS = { x: 187.5, y: 170 }, C_POS = { x: 272.5, y: 88 };
  const LEAK_X = 395, SYN_X = 470, F1_Y = 244;

  // --- redox ladder (true E°′ spacing on the y axis) ---------------------------------------
  type Rung = { label: string; volts: number; x: number };
  const LADDER: Rung[] = [
    { label: 'NADH', volts: -0.32, x: 40 },
    { label: 'FMN', volts: -0.30, x: 105 },
    { label: 'Fe-S', volts: 0.00, x: 170 },
    { label: 'CoQ', volts: 0.04, x: 240 },
    { label: 'cyt c', volts: 0.25, x: 320 },
    { label: 'cyt a', volts: 0.29, x: 395 },
    { label: 'O₂', volts: 0.82, x: 480 },
  ];
  const ly = (v: number) => 374 + (v + 0.35) * (114 / 1.2);

  // deterministic scatter of H+ positions in the intermembrane space
  const DOTS: { x: number; y: number }[] = (() => {
    const out: { x: number; y: number }[] = [];
    let seed = 7;
    const rnd = () => { seed = (seed * 9301 + 49297) % 233280; return seed / 233280; };
    // keep clear of the pump arrows + their labels, the synthase inlet, and cytochrome c
    const clear = (x: number, y: number) =>
      ![60, 230, 315].some((cx) => x > cx - 11 && x < cx + 40) && !(x > 459 && x < 481) && !(x > 258 && x < 287 && y > 70);
    let tries = 0;
    while (out.length < MAX_H && tries < 20000) {
      tries++;
      const x = 12 + rnd() * 516, y = 30 + rnd() * 52;
      if (!clear(x, y)) continue;
      const gap = tries > 8000 ? 9 : 14;
      if (out.every((d) => Math.hypot(d.x - x, d.y - y) > gap)) out.push({ x, y });
    }
    while (out.length < MAX_H) out.push({ x: 20 + out.length * 15, y: 80 }); // never reached; safety
    return out;
  })();

  type Pt = { x: number; y: number };
  type Stop = { p: Pt; rung: number; cx?: Cx };

  function blockAt(entry: Entry, inhib: Inhib): Cx | null {
    if (inhib === 'I') return entry === 'NADH' ? 'I' : null; // FADH2 enters downstream of I
    if (inhib === 'III') return 'III';
    if (inhib === 'IV') return 'IV';
    return null;
  }

  function pathFor(entry: Entry, block: Cx | null): Stop[] {
    const full: Stop[] = entry === 'NADH'
      ? [
          { p: { x: CXX.I, y: 250 }, rung: 0 },
          { p: { x: CXX.I, y: E_Y }, rung: 2, cx: 'I' },
          { p: Q_POS, rung: 3 },
          { p: { x: CXX.III, y: E_Y }, rung: 3.5, cx: 'III' },
          { p: C_POS, rung: 4 },
          { p: { x: CXX.IV, y: E_Y }, rung: 5, cx: 'IV' },
          { p: { x: CXX.IV, y: 238 }, rung: 6 },
        ]
      : [
          { p: { x: CXX.II, y: 250 }, rung: 3 },
          { p: { x: CXX.II, y: E_Y }, rung: 3, cx: 'II' },
          { p: Q_POS, rung: 3 },
          { p: { x: CXX.III, y: E_Y }, rung: 3.5, cx: 'III' },
          { p: C_POS, rung: 4 },
          { p: { x: CXX.IV, y: E_Y }, rung: 5, cx: 'IV' },
          { p: { x: CXX.IV, y: 238 }, rung: 6 },
        ];
    if (!block) return full;
    // electrons advance up to the blocked complex and pile up there
    const i = full.findIndex((st) => st.cx === block);
    const cut = full.slice(0, i + 1).map((st) => ({ ...st }));
    const last = cut[cut.length - 1];
    last.rung = block === 'I' ? 0 : block === 'III' ? 3 : 5; // where the pile-up sits on the ladder
    last.cx = undefined; // a blocked complex does not pump
    return cut;
  }

  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  type View = {
    entry: Entry; inhib: Inhib; uncouple: boolean; pairs: number;
    dots: { x: number; y: number; moving?: boolean }[];
    electron: Pt | null; ladderPos: number | null;
    activeCx: Cx | null; rotor: number; synthRunning: boolean; leaking: boolean;
  };

  function upArrow(g: SVGElement, x: number, y1: number, y2: number, color: string, w = 3): void {
    g.appendChild(el('line', { x1: x, y1, x2: x, y2: y2 + 7, stroke: color, 'stroke-width': w, 'stroke-linecap': 'round' }));
    g.appendChild(el('path', { d: `M${x - 6},${y2 + 9} L${x},${y2} L${x + 6},${y2 + 9} Z`, fill: color }));
  }
  function downArrow(g: SVGElement, x: number, y1: number, y2: number, color: string, w = 3, dash?: string): void {
    const a: Record<string, string | number> = { x1: x, y1, x2: x, y2: y2 - 7, stroke: color, 'stroke-width': w, 'stroke-linecap': 'round' };
    if (dash) a['stroke-dasharray'] = dash;
    g.appendChild(el('line', a));
    g.appendChild(el('path', { d: `M${x - 6},${y2 - 9} L${x},${y2} L${x + 6},${y2 - 9} Z`, fill: color }));
  }

  function drawScene(svg: SVGElement, v: View): void {
    const w = svg.getBoundingClientRect().width;
    FS = w > 0 && w < 480 ? 1.3 : 1;
    const g = el('g', {});
    const block = blockAt(v.entry, v.inhib);
    const flowing = !block;
    const cycled = v.pairs > 0;

    // ---- compartments
    g.appendChild(el('rect', { x: 0, y: 0, width: W, height: IMS_BOT, fill: '#fbf6ea' }));
    g.appendChild(el('rect', { x: 0, y: MEM_TOP, width: W, height: MEM_BOT - MEM_TOP, fill: '#e9ecf4' }));
    g.appendChild(el('rect', { x: 0, y: MEM_BOT, width: W, height: MAT_BOT - MEM_BOT, fill: '#eef6f6' }));
    for (let x = 4; x < W; x += 9) {
      g.appendChild(el('circle', { cx: x, cy: MEM_TOP + 4, r: 3.4, fill: '#cfd5e4' }));
      g.appendChild(el('circle', { cx: x, cy: MEM_BOT - 4, r: 3.4, fill: '#cfd5e4' }));
    }
    g.appendChild(el('text', { x: 8, y: 16, fill: INK, 'font-size': 11 * FS, 'font-weight': 700, 'letter-spacing': '0.04em' }, FS > 1 ? 'INTERMEMBRANE SPACE · high [H⁺]' : 'INTERMEMBRANE SPACE · high [H⁺], + side'));
    g.appendChild(el('text', { x: 8, y: MAT_BOT - 8, fill: ACCENT, 'font-size': 11 * FS, 'font-weight': 700, 'letter-spacing': '0.04em' }, FS > 1 ? 'MATRIX · low [H⁺]' : 'MATRIX · low [H⁺], − side'));
    if (!v.uncouple) {
      g.appendChild(el('text', { x: LEAK_X, y: MEM_TOP + 40, 'text-anchor': 'middle', fill: MUTED, 'font-size': 10 * FS, 'font-style': 'italic' }, 'inner'));
      g.appendChild(el('text', { x: LEAK_X, y: MEM_TOP + 52, 'text-anchor': 'middle', fill: MUTED, 'font-size': 10 * FS, 'font-style': 'italic' }, 'membrane'));
    }

    // ---- complexes
    const subs: Record<Cx, string> = { I: 'NADH → Q', II: 'succ. → Q', III: 'Q → cyt c', IV: 'cyt c → O₂' };
    (['I', 'II', 'III', 'IV'] as Cx[]).forEach((c) => {
      const x = CXX[c];
      const bypassed = (c === 'I' && v.entry === 'FADH2') || (c === 'II' && v.entry === 'NADH');
      const isBlocked = block === c;
      const active = v.activeCx === c;
      const stroke = isBlocked ? RED : active ? ACCENT : NAVY;
      g.appendChild(el('rect', {
        x: x - CW / 2, y: C_TOP, width: CW, height: C_BOT - C_TOP, rx: 12,
        fill: active ? ACCENT : isBlocked ? '#fbe9e7' : '#dfe3ee', 'fill-opacity': active ? 0.9 : 1,
        stroke, 'stroke-width': active || isBlocked ? 2.5 : 1.5, opacity: bypassed ? 0.45 : 1,
      }));
      g.appendChild(el('text', { x, y: C_TOP + 36, 'text-anchor': 'middle', fill: active ? '#fff' : isBlocked ? RED : NAVY, 'font-size': 20 * FS, 'font-weight': 800, opacity: bypassed ? 0.5 : 1 }, c));
      g.appendChild(el('text', { x, y: C_TOP + 52, 'text-anchor': 'middle', fill: active ? '#fff' : INK, 'font-size': 9.5 * FS, opacity: bypassed ? 0.5 : 1 }, subs[c]));
      if (isBlocked) {
        g.appendChild(el('path', { d: `M${x - 9},${E_Y - 9} L${x + 9},${E_Y + 9} M${x + 9},${E_Y - 9} L${x - 9},${E_Y + 9}`, stroke: RED, 'stroke-width': 4, 'stroke-linecap': 'round' }));
      }
      // pump arrows with their stoichiometry
      const pumps = PUMP[c];
      if (c === 'II') {
        if (v.entry === 'FADH2') g.appendChild(el('text', { x, y: 60, 'text-anchor': 'middle', fill: MUTED, 'font-size': 11 * FS, 'font-weight': 700 }, '0 H⁺'));
        return;
      }
      if (bypassed) return;
      const path = pathFor(v.entry, null);
      const reached = !block || path.findIndex((s) => s.cx === c) < path.findIndex((s) => s.cx === block);
      const op = flowing && reached ? 1 : 0.22;
      const ag = el('g', { opacity: op });
      upArrow(ag, x, C_TOP - 4, 42, GOLD);
      ag.appendChild(el('text', { x: x + 9, y: 54, fill: GOLD_INK, 'font-size': 11 * FS, 'font-weight': 800 }, `${pumps} H⁺`));
      g.appendChild(ag);
    });

    // ---- mobile carriers: crossover colouring
    const qReduced = block === 'III' || block === 'IV' || (flowing && cycled);
    const cReduced = block === 'IV' || (flowing && cycled);
    const carrier = (p: Pt, label: string, reduced: boolean) => {
      g.appendChild(el('circle', { cx: p.x, cy: p.y, r: 11, fill: reduced ? ACCENT : SLATE, stroke: '#fff', 'stroke-width': 2 }));
      g.appendChild(el('text', { x: p.x, y: p.y + 4, 'text-anchor': 'middle', fill: '#fff', 'font-size': 11 * FS, 'font-weight': 800 }, label));
    };
    carrier(Q_POS, 'Q', qReduced);
    carrier(C_POS, 'c', cReduced);

    // ---- electron entry + O2 labels in the matrix
    g.appendChild(el('text', { x: CXX.I, y: 214, 'text-anchor': 'middle', fill: v.entry === 'NADH' ? ORANGE : FAINT, 'font-size': 10.5 * FS, 'font-weight': 700 }, 'NADH → NAD⁺'));
    g.appendChild(el('text', { x: CXX.II, y: FS > 1 ? 232 : 214, 'text-anchor': 'middle', fill: v.entry === 'FADH2' ? ORANGE : FAINT, 'font-size': 10.5 * FS, 'font-weight': 700 }, 'FADH₂ → FAD'));
    g.appendChild(el('text', { x: CXX.IV, y: 214, 'text-anchor': 'middle', fill: flowing ? ACCENT : FAINT, 'font-size': 10.5 * FS, 'font-weight': 700 }, '½O₂ + 2H⁺ → H₂O'));

    // ---- uncoupler leak channel
    if (v.uncouple) {
      g.appendChild(el('rect', { x: LEAK_X - 17, y: MEM_TOP + 52, width: 34, height: 18, rx: 5, fill: ORANGE }));
      g.appendChild(el('text', { x: LEAK_X, y: MEM_TOP + 65, 'text-anchor': 'middle', fill: '#fff', 'font-size': 10 * FS, 'font-weight': 800 }, 'DNP'));
      downArrow(g, LEAK_X, 60, MEM_TOP + 50, ORANGE, 2.5, '5 4');
      downArrow(g, LEAK_X, MEM_TOP + 72, 226, ORANGE, 2.5, '5 4');
      g.appendChild(el('text', { x: LEAK_X, y: 242, 'text-anchor': 'middle', fill: ORANGE, 'font-size': 10.5 * FS, 'font-weight': 800 }, 'H⁺ leak'));
      g.appendChild(el('text', { x: LEAK_X, y: 255, 'text-anchor': 'middle', fill: ORANGE, 'font-size': 10.5 * FS, 'font-weight': 800 }, '→ heat'));
    }

    // ---- ATP synthase (F0 in the membrane, F1 head in the matrix)
    const synCol = v.uncouple ? ORANGE : GOLD;
    g.appendChild(el('text', { x: SYN_X, y: 18, 'text-anchor': 'middle', fill: v.uncouple ? ORANGE : GOLD_INK, 'font-size': 11 * FS, 'font-weight': 800 }, 'ATP synthase'));
    downArrow(g, SYN_X, 26, MEM_TOP - 2, synCol, v.synthRunning ? 4 : 2.5);
    g.appendChild(el('rect', { x: SYN_X - 20, y: MEM_TOP + 4, width: 40, height: MEM_BOT - MEM_TOP - 8, rx: 10, fill: '#f5ecd2', stroke: synCol, 'stroke-width': 2 }));
    for (let k = -12; k <= 12; k += 8) g.appendChild(el('line', { x1: SYN_X + k, y1: MEM_TOP + 10, x2: SYN_X + k, y2: MEM_BOT - 10, stroke: synCol, 'stroke-opacity': 0.5, 'stroke-width': 1.5 }));
    g.appendChild(el('line', { x1: SYN_X + 27, y1: MEM_TOP + 40, x2: SYN_X + 27, y2: F1_Y - 16, stroke: '#b9a878', 'stroke-width': 5, 'stroke-linecap': 'round' }));
    g.appendChild(el('line', { x1: SYN_X, y1: MEM_BOT - 4, x2: SYN_X, y2: F1_Y, stroke: NAVY, 'stroke-width': 5 }));
    g.appendChild(el('circle', { cx: SYN_X, cy: F1_Y, r: 29, fill: '#fbf3dc', stroke: synCol, 'stroke-width': 2 }));
    for (let k = 0; k < 6; k++) {
      const a = (k * 60 - 90) * Math.PI / 180;
      g.appendChild(el('circle', { cx: SYN_X + 18 * Math.cos(a), cy: F1_Y + 18 * Math.sin(a), r: 9, fill: k % 2 ? '#efe0b4' : '#f8eed3', stroke: '#c9a94a', 'stroke-width': 1 }));
    }
    const rg = el('g', { transform: `rotate(${v.rotor.toFixed(2)} ${SYN_X} ${F1_Y})` });
    rg.appendChild(el('line', { x1: SYN_X, y1: F1_Y, x2: SYN_X, y2: F1_Y - 15, stroke: NAVY, 'stroke-width': 4.5, 'stroke-linecap': 'round' }));
    rg.appendChild(el('circle', { cx: SYN_X, cy: F1_Y, r: 4.5, fill: NAVY }));
    g.appendChild(rg);
    g.appendChild(el('text', { x: SYN_X, y: 288, 'text-anchor': 'middle', fill: v.uncouple ? ORANGE : GOLD_INK, 'font-size': 10.5 * FS, 'font-weight': 700 }, v.uncouple ? 'bypassed: no ATP' : 'ADP + Pᵢ → ATP'));

    // ---- protons in the IMS (and in flight)
    v.dots.forEach((d) => {
      g.appendChild(el('circle', { cx: d.x, cy: d.y, r: d.moving ? 4.2 : 3.6, fill: GOLD, stroke: d.moving ? GOLD_INK : 'none', 'stroke-width': 1 }));
    });

    // ---- the electron pair
    if (v.electron) {
      g.appendChild(el('circle', { cx: v.electron.x, cy: v.electron.y, r: 8, fill: ORANGE, stroke: '#fff', 'stroke-width': 2 }));
      g.appendChild(el('text', { x: v.electron.x, y: v.electron.y + 3.5, 'text-anchor': 'middle', fill: '#fff', 'font-size': 9 * FS, 'font-weight': 800 }, '2e⁻'));
    }

    // ---- redox ladder panel
    const L = el('g', {});
    L.appendChild(el('rect', { x: 0, y: 306, width: W, height: 202, fill: '#ffffff' }));
    L.appendChild(el('line', { x1: 0, y1: 306, x2: W, y2: 306, stroke: FAINT, 'stroke-width': 1 }));
    const title = el('text', { x: 8, y: 324, fill: NAVY, 'font-size': 11.5 * FS, 'font-weight': 800 });
    title.appendChild(el('tspan', {}, 'Redox ladder'));
    title.appendChild(el('tspan', { fill: INK, 'font-weight': 400 }, ' — electrons fall toward more positive E°′ (volts)'));
    L.appendChild(title);
    const bands: { from: number; to: number; label: string; cx: Cx }[] = [
      { from: 18, to: 240, label: v.entry === 'FADH2' ? 'Complex I — skipped by FADH₂' : 'Complex I → pumps 4 H⁺', cx: 'I' },
      { from: 240, to: 320, label: 'III → 4 H⁺', cx: 'III' },
      { from: 320, to: 505, label: 'Complex IV → 2 H⁺', cx: 'IV' },
    ];
    bands.forEach((b, i) => {
      L.appendChild(el('rect', { x: b.from, y: 332, width: b.to - b.from, height: 168, fill: i % 2 ? '#f3f5fa' : '#fafbfd', opacity: b.cx === 'I' && v.entry === 'FADH2' ? 0.5 : 1 }));
      L.appendChild(el('text', { x: (b.from + b.to) / 2, y: 346, 'text-anchor': 'middle', fill: b.cx === 'I' && v.entry === 'FADH2' ? MUTED : GOLD_INK, 'font-size': 10 * FS, 'font-weight': 700 }, b.label));
    });
    const endRung = pathFor(v.entry, block).slice(-1)[0].rung;
    const startRung = v.entry === 'NADH' ? 0 : 3;
    for (let i = 0; i < LADDER.length; i++) {
      const r = LADDER[i];
      const y = ly(r.volts);
      const live = i >= startRung && (!block || i <= endRung);
      const op = live ? 1 : 0.35;
      if (i < LADDER.length - 1) {
        const n = LADDER[i + 1];
        L.appendChild(el('path', { d: `M${r.x + 22},${y} L${n.x - 22},${ly(n.volts)}`, stroke: FAINT, 'stroke-width': 1.5, 'stroke-dasharray': '3 3', fill: 'none', opacity: op }));
      }
      L.appendChild(el('line', { x1: r.x - 22, y1: y, x2: r.x + 22, y2: y, stroke: live ? NAVY : SLATE, 'stroke-width': 3, 'stroke-linecap': 'round', opacity: op }));
      L.appendChild(el('text', { x: r.x, y: y - 9, 'text-anchor': 'middle', fill: NAVY, 'font-size': 10.5 * FS, 'font-weight': 700, opacity: op }, r.label));
      L.appendChild(el('text', { x: r.x, y: y + 13, 'text-anchor': 'middle', fill: INK, 'font-size': 9.5 * FS, 'font-family': 'ui-monospace, monospace', opacity: op }, `${r.volts > 0 ? '+' : r.volts < 0 ? '−' : ''}${Math.abs(r.volts).toFixed(2)}`));
    }
    if (v.entry === 'FADH2') {
      L.appendChild(el('text', { x: 240, y: 380, 'text-anchor': 'middle', fill: ORANGE, 'font-size': 10 * FS, 'font-weight': 700 }, 'FADH₂ joins here'));
    }
    if (block) {
      const r = LADDER[Math.floor(endRung)];
      const x = r.x + 32, y = ly(r.volts) + 8;
      L.appendChild(el('path', { d: `M${x - 6},${y - 6} L${x + 6},${y + 6} M${x + 6},${y - 6} L${x - 6},${y + 6}`, stroke: RED, 'stroke-width': 3, 'stroke-linecap': 'round' }));
    }
    if (v.ladderPos !== null) {
      const i = Math.min(LADDER.length - 1, Math.floor(v.ladderPos));
      const j = Math.min(LADDER.length - 1, i + 1);
      const f = v.ladderPos - i;
      const x = LADDER[i].x + (LADDER[j].x - LADDER[i].x) * f;
      const y = ly(LADDER[i].volts) + (ly(LADDER[j].volts) - ly(LADDER[i].volts)) * f;
      L.appendChild(el('circle', { cx: x, cy: y, r: 5.5, fill: ORANGE, stroke: '#fff', 'stroke-width': 1.5 }));
    }
    g.appendChild(L);

    svg.replaceChildren(g);
  }

  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  const ease = (t: number) => (t < 0.5 ? 4 * t * t * t : 1 - Math.pow(-2 * t + 2, 3) / 2);
  const clamp01 = (t: number) => Math.max(0, Math.min(1, t));
  const lerp = (a: Pt, b: Pt, t: number): Pt => ({ x: a.x + (b.x - a.x) * t, y: a.y + (b.y - a.y) * t });
  const fmtHalf = (halves: number) => (halves % 2 === 0 ? String(halves / 2) : `${Math.floor(halves / 2) > 0 ? Math.floor(halves / 2) : ''}½`);

  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-pgbattery]').forEach((root) => {
    const svg = root.querySelector('[data-stage]') as unknown as SVGElement;
    const pmfNum = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-pmf-num]')!;
    const bar = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-bar]')!;
    const thresh = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-thresh]')!;
    const atpEl = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-atp]')!;
    const o2El = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-o2]')!;
    const heatEl = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-heat]')!;
    const yieldEl = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-yield]')!;
    const logEl = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-log]')!;
    const takeawayEl = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-takeaway]')!;
    const runBtn = root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-run]')!;
    const resetBtn = root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-reset]')!;
    const uncoupleBtn = root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-uncouple]')!;
    const entryBtns = root.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-entry]');
    const inhibBtns = root.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-inhib]');
    thresh.style.left = `${(THRESH / MAX_H) * 100}%`;

    const s = {
      entry: 'NADH' as Entry, inhib: 'none' as Inhib, uncouple: false,
      hPlus: 0, atp: 0, heat: 0, o2Halves: 0, pairs: 0, rotor: 0,
      endRung: null as number | null,
    };

    type Plan = {
      stops: Stop[]; pumps: { cx: Cx; n: number; t: number; first: number }[];
      h0: number; hPeak: number; hAfter: number; atpMade: number; leaked: number; reachesO2: boolean;
      tElec: number; tSettle: number; tEnd: number;
    };
    let anim: { plan: Plan; t0: number; raf: number } | null = null;

    function pumpedPerPair(): number {
      if (blockAt(s.entry, s.inhib)) return 0;
      return s.entry === 'NADH' ? PUMP.I + PUMP.III + PUMP.IV : PUMP.II + PUMP.III + PUMP.IV;
    }

    function staticView(): View {
      const dots = DOTS.slice(0, Math.min(MAX_H, s.hPlus)).map((d) => ({ ...d }));
      return {
        entry: s.entry, inhib: s.inhib, uncouple: s.uncouple, pairs: s.pairs, dots,
        electron: null, ladderPos: s.endRung, activeCx: null, rotor: s.rotor, synthRunning: false, leaking: false,
      };
    }

    function setMeter(h: number): void {
      pmfNum.textContent = `${Math.round(h)} H⁺`;
      bar.style.width = `${Math.min(100, (h / MAX_H) * 100)}%`;
      bar.classList.toggle('is-above', h > THRESH);
    }

    function takeaway(): string {
      if (s.inhib === 'IV') {
        return 'Cyanide jams Complex IV: electrons pile up behind it (every carrier stays reduced), O₂ can no longer be reduced, and the whole chain stalls. The pumps stop, the gradient cannot be recharged, and ATP synthesis stops — this is why cyanide kills in minutes. The mitochondria are full of fuel and oxygen and still cannot make energy.';
      }
      if (s.inhib === 'III') {
        return 'Antimycin A blocks Complex III: CoQ upstream stays reduced while cyt c downstream stays oxidized — the classic crossover point. With nowhere to send its electrons, Complex I stalls too, so pumping stops, no O₂ is consumed, and ATP output collapses.';
      }
      if (s.inhib === 'I' && s.entry === 'NADH') {
        return 'Rotenone blocks Complex I, so NADH electrons cannot get in at all — flow is dead on arrival, and the carriers downstream stay oxidized. (Switch the entry point to FADH₂: those electrons enter at Complex II, downstream of the block, and flow resumes.)';
      }
      if (s.uncouple) {
        return 'Uncoupler engaged: the pumps still work, but the protons skip ATP synthase and leak straight back across the membrane. Electrons still flow and O₂ is still consumed — the energy comes out as HEAT, not ATP. This is brown fat warming a newborn, and the lethal logic of the DNP diet pill.';
      }
      const lead = s.inhib === 'I' && s.entry === 'FADH2'
        ? 'Rotenone blocks Complex I — but FADH₂ enters at Complex II, downstream of the block, so its electrons flow on untouched. Where flow stops tells you where the block is. '
        : '';
      if (s.pairs === 0) {
        return `${lead}Idle. The chain is loaded but no electrons are moving. Send an electron pair and watch the pumps charge the battery.`;
      }
      if (s.atp === 0) {
        return `${lead}Charging: the pumps have stored ${s.hPlus} H⁺, but ATP synthase only turns once the gradient is above the threshold. Send another pair.`;
      }
      const n = pumpedPerPair();
      return `${lead}Coupled and running. Each ${s.entry === 'NADH' ? 'NADH' : 'FADH₂'} pair pumps ${n} H⁺${s.entry === 'FADH2' ? ' (it skips Complex I, and Complex II pumps none)' : ''}; at ~4 H⁺ per ATP that buys ~${(n / H_PER_ATP).toFixed(1)} ATP. The first pair only charged the battery, so the running total lags — keep sending pairs and ATP ÷ pairs climbs toward ${(n / H_PER_ATP).toFixed(1)}.`;
    }

    function statusClass(): void {
      const coupled = !blockAt(s.entry, s.inhib) && !s.uncouple && s.atp > 0;
      takeawayEl.classList.toggle('pgb-ok', coupled);
      takeawayEl.classList.toggle('pgb-bad', !!blockAt(s.entry, s.inhib) || s.uncouple);
    }

    function refresh(): void {
      setMeter(s.hPlus);
      atpEl.textContent = String(s.atp);
      o2El.textContent = fmtHalf(s.o2Halves);
      heatEl.textContent = String(s.heat);
      const n = pumpedPerPair();
      yieldEl.textContent = n === 0 ? '0 H⁺ → 0 ATP'
        : s.uncouple ? `${n} H⁺ → leak, 0 ATP`
          : `${n} H⁺ ÷ 4 = ${(n / H_PER_ATP).toFixed(1)} ATP`;
      takeawayEl.textContent = takeaway();
      statusClass();
      drawScene(svg, staticView());
    }

    function makePlan(): Plan {
      const block = blockAt(s.entry, s.inhib);
      const stops = pathFor(s.entry, block);
      const seg = 190;
      const tElec = (stops.length - 1) * seg;
      const pumps: Plan['pumps'] = [];
      let cum = 0;
      // a blocked chain has no steady electron flow, so no complex pumps (not even the ones upstream)
      if (!block) stops.forEach((st, i) => {
        if (st.cx && PUMP[st.cx] > 0) { pumps.push({ cx: st.cx, n: PUMP[st.cx], t: i * seg, first: cum }); cum += PUMP[st.cx]; }
      });
      const h0 = s.hPlus, hPeak = Math.min(MAX_H, h0 + cum);
      let atpMade = 0, leaked = 0, hAfter = hPeak;
      if (s.uncouple) { leaked = hPeak; hAfter = 0; }
      else { atpMade = Math.max(0, Math.floor((hPeak - THRESH) / H_PER_ATP)); hAfter = hPeak - atpMade * H_PER_ATP; }
      const leaving = hPeak - hAfter;
      const tSettle = tElec + 380;
      const tEnd = tSettle + (leaving > 0 ? 520 + leaving * 45 : 200);
      return { stops, pumps, h0, hPeak, hAfter, atpMade, leaked, reachesO2: !block, tElec, tSettle, tEnd };
    }

    function commit(p: Plan): void {
      s.pairs += p.reachesO2 ? 1 : 0;
      s.hPlus = p.hAfter;
      s.atp += p.atpMade;
      s.heat += p.leaked;
      if (p.reachesO2) s.o2Halves += 1;
      s.rotor = (s.rotor + 120 * p.atpMade) % 360;
      s.endRung = p.stops[p.stops.length - 1].rung;
      const pumped = p.hPeak - p.h0;
      const who = s.entry === 'NADH' ? 'NADH' : 'FADH₂';
      logEl.textContent = !p.reachesO2
        ? `No flow: the ${who} electrons stop at the blocked complex — 0 H⁺ pumped, no O₂ used, no ATP.`
        : s.uncouple
          ? `Pair ${s.pairs} (${who}): ${pumped} H⁺ pumped, ½ O₂ reduced to water — and every proton leaked back as heat. 0 ATP.`
          : `Pair ${s.pairs} (${who}): ${pumped} H⁺ pumped, ½ O₂ reduced to water, ${p.atpMade} ATP made; ${p.hAfter} H⁺ left in the gradient.`;
      refresh();
    }

    function frame(now: number): void {
      if (!anim) return;
      const p = anim.plan, t = now - anim.t0;
      // electron position along its stops
      const segs = p.stops.length - 1;
      const fe = clamp01(t / p.tElec) * segs;
      const si = Math.min(segs - 1, Math.floor(fe));
      const sf = ease(fe - si);
      const done = t >= p.tElec;
      const a = p.stops[si], b = p.stops[si + 1];
      const electron = done ? null : lerp(a.p, b.p, sf);
      const ladderPos = done ? p.stops[segs].rung : a.rung + (b.rung - a.rung) * sf;
      const activeCx = done ? null : (sf > 0.8 ? b.cx : a.cx) ?? null;

      // protons: rising from pumps, then leaving through the synthase or the leak
      const dots: View['dots'] = [];
      let present = p.h0;
      for (let i = 0; i < p.h0; i++) dots.push({ ...DOTS[i] });
      p.pumps.forEach((pu) => {
        for (let k = 0; k < pu.n; k++) {
          const idx = p.h0 + pu.first + k;
          if (idx >= MAX_H) continue;
          const st = t - pu.t - k * 55;
          if (st < 0) continue;
          const f = ease(clamp01(st / 420));
          const from = { x: CXX[pu.cx] + (k - (pu.n - 1) / 2) * 7, y: C_TOP + 6 };
          if (f < 1) dots.push({ ...lerp(from, DOTS[idx], f), moving: true });
          else { dots.push({ ...DOTS[idx] }); present++; }
        }
      });
      const leaving = p.hPeak - p.hAfter;
      const exitX = s.uncouple ? LEAK_X : SYN_X;
      if (t >= p.tSettle && leaving > 0) {
        for (let m = 0; m < leaving; m++) {
          const idx = p.hPeak - 1 - m;
          const st = t - p.tSettle - m * 45;
          const di = dots.findIndex((d) => d.x === DOTS[idx].x && d.y === DOTS[idx].y);
          if (st < 0 || di < 0) continue;
          const f = clamp01(st / 520);
          dots.splice(di, 1);
          present--;
          if (f < 1) {
            const mid = { x: exitX, y: 44 }, end = { x: exitX, y: s.uncouple ? 226 : MEM_BOT - 6 };
            const pos = f < 0.5 ? lerp(DOTS[idx], mid, ease(f * 2)) : lerp(mid, end, ease((f - 0.5) * 2));
            dots.push({ ...pos, moving: true });
          }
        }
      }
      const sp = clamp01((t - p.tSettle) / Math.max(1, p.tEnd - p.tSettle - 120));
      const rotor = s.rotor + 120 * p.atpMade * ease(sp);
      setMeter(present);
      if (p.atpMade > 0) atpEl.textContent = String(s.atp + Math.floor(p.atpMade * sp + 1e-6));
      if (p.leaked > 0) heatEl.textContent = String(s.heat + Math.round(p.leaked * sp));

      drawScene(svg, {
        entry: s.entry, inhib: s.inhib, uncouple: s.uncouple, pairs: s.pairs + (done && p.reachesO2 ? 1 : 0), dots,
        electron, ladderPos, activeCx, rotor, synthRunning: t >= p.tSettle && p.atpMade > 0, leaking: s.uncouple,
      });
      if (t >= p.tEnd) { const pl = p; anim = null; commit(pl); return; }
      anim.raf = requestAnimationFrame(frame);
    }

    function finishAnim(): void {
      if (!anim) return;
      cancelAnimationFrame(anim.raf);
      const p = anim.plan; anim = null; commit(p);
    }

    function runPair(): void {
      finishAnim();
      const plan = makePlan();
      const reduce = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
      if (reduce) { commit(plan); return; }
      anim = { plan, t0: performance.now(), raf: 0 };
      anim.raf = requestAnimationFrame(frame);
    }

    function setEntry(entry: Entry): void {
      finishAnim();
      s.entry = entry; s.endRung = null;
      entryBtns.forEach((b) => b.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(b.dataset.entry === entry)));
      logEl.textContent = '';
      refresh();
    }

    function setInhib(inhib: Inhib): void {
      finishAnim();
      s.inhib = inhib; s.endRung = null;
      inhibBtns.forEach((b) => b.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(b.dataset.inhib === inhib)));
      logEl.textContent = '';
      refresh();
    }

    function setUncouple(on: boolean): void {
      finishAnim();
      s.uncouple = on;
      uncoupleBtn.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(on));
      uncoupleBtn.textContent = `DNP / proton leak: ${on ? 'ON' : 'OFF'}`;
      if (on && s.hPlus > 0) {
        // the stored gradient immediately leaks away as heat
        logEl.textContent = `The ${s.hPlus} H⁺ already stored leak straight back through the uncoupler as heat.`;
        s.heat += s.hPlus;
        s.hPlus = 0;
      } else logEl.textContent = '';
      refresh();
    }

    function resetAll(): void {
      if (anim) { cancelAnimationFrame(anim.raf); anim = null; }
      Object.assign(s, { entry: 'NADH', inhib: 'none', uncouple: false, hPlus: 0, atp: 0, heat: 0, o2Halves: 0, pairs: 0, rotor: 0, endRung: null });
      entryBtns.forEach((b) => b.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(b.dataset.entry === 'NADH')));
      inhibBtns.forEach((b) => b.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(b.dataset.inhib === 'none')));
      uncoupleBtn.setAttribute('aria-pressed', 'false');
      uncoupleBtn.textContent = 'DNP / proton leak: OFF';
      logEl.textContent = '';
      refresh();
    }

    entryBtns.forEach((b) => b.addEventListener('click', () => setEntry(b.dataset.entry as Entry)));
    inhibBtns.forEach((b) => b.addEventListener('click', () => setInhib(b.dataset.inhib as Inhib)));
    uncoupleBtn.addEventListener('click', () => setUncouple(!s.uncouple));
    runBtn.addEventListener('click', runPair);
    resetBtn.addEventListener('click', resetAll);

    // re-lay the text when the figure crosses the phone breakpoint (rotation, window resize)
    if ('ResizeObserver' in window) {
      let lastFs = 0;
      new ResizeObserver(() => {
        const w = svg.getBoundingClientRect().width;
        const f = w > 0 && w < 480 ? 1.3 : 1;
        if (f !== lastFs) { lastFs = f; if (!anim) drawScene(svg, staticView()); }
      }).observe(svg as unknown as Element);
    }

    refresh();
  });
</script>

<style>
  .pgb { padding: var(--ddp-space-3) var(--ddp-space-4) var(--ddp-space-4); margin: var(--ddp-space-5) 0; }
  .pgb-head { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; gap: 0.3rem; font-weight: 600; font-size: var(--ddp-text-sm); color: var(--ddp-color-primary); margin-bottom: var(--ddp-space-2); }
  .pgb-chip { font-family: var(--ddp-font-mono); font-size: var(--ddp-text-xs); font-weight: 400; color: var(--ddp-color-muted); }
  .pgb-howto { margin: 0 0 var(--ddp-space-2); font-size: var(--ddp-text-xs); color: var(--ddp-color-ink-soft); line-height: 1.5; }
